# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12 (Q45): a `for:` in a named Structure's body is a statement of the body,
# as in a method's body.  Two executions from the root: n counts 3 at each (its declaration runs again).  total
# is Counter's hidden input -- a procedure without arguments is one with hidden arguments (the author,
# 2026-09-28, OPUS-CODEX-20260928-08) -- from the root's 0 at each execution: `total 3` twice; the bare write
# changes only Counter's value (Q52), and the root's total at its place of declaration (gt's node\total) stays
# 0.  Entry 7.
size_t: total 0U
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    for: int(i, 0) (i < 3) i++
        n: n + 1U
        total: total + 1U
    end: for
    c.printf: "total %zu\n" total
return
fn: gt () size_t
    return: node\total
end: gt
Counter
Counter
size_t: t 9U
t: gt()
int: ok 0
if: Counter\n = 3U && t = 0U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
